// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_SECRET_EXFILTRATION
// D3: the same field read through a FUNCTION-VALUE ALIAS. Resolved by reusing the binding's
// `fn_alias` — the resolution the summary lookups already perform — rather than adding a second
// alias path.
// Worth stating as a rule: aliasing has now laundered THREE separate mechanisms in this codebase
// (interprocedural sinks, declared return qualifiers, and this). Any new name-keyed lookup should
// resolve the alias first as a matter of course, not as a follow-up fix after an adversary finds it.
struct V { k: secret<i64> }
fn get() -> V { return V { k: 42 }; }
fn main() { let g = get; print(g().k); }
